@startuml sequence_import_rerun
!theme plain
title Experiment Import & Re-Run – Browse -> Backend -> Setup

actor User
participant "Browse Page\n(Streamlit)" as Browse
participant "FastAPI\n/app.py" as API
participant "export_import.py\n(validator + extractor)" as EI
participant "db.py\n(SQLite WAL)" as DB
participant "File System\n(results)" as FS
participant "Setup Page\n(Streamlit)" as Setup

== Import ZIP ==
User -> Browse: upload .zip file\n(st.file_uploader)
Browse -> API: POST /experiments/import\n(multipart: zip file)
API -> EI: validate_import_zip(zip_path, results_root)

group Validation
    EI -> EI: check: valid zip?
    EI -> EI: check: deap_export_manifest.json present?
    EI -> EI: check: schema_version <= current?
    EI -> EI: check: run_dirs have manifest.json?
    EI -> EI: check: path traversal? (.., absolute paths)
    EI -> EI: check: disk space? (shutil.disk_usage)
end

alt validation failed
    EI --> API: ImportValidationResult(ok=False, errors=[...])
    API --> Browse: 422 {errors: [{path, code, message}], warnings: [...]}
    Browse --> User: render errors inline
else validation ok
    EI -> FS: extract_import_zip(zip_path, results_root)
    note right of FS: preserve dir structure\nskip/overwrite duplicates
    EI -> DB: restore_experiment_to_db(experiment.json, run_dirs)
    DB -> DB: insert_experiment(origin='import')
    note right of DB: Import restores the *archived* status,\nnot always 'completed' —\ncompleted -> set_completed\ncancelled -> set_cancelled\nfailed -> set_failed(archived error)\nqueued/running -> set_failed\n("...original process no longer exists")\nthen restore_timestamps(created_at/started_at/finished_at)\nparsed back from the archived ISO strings
    EI --> API: {imported: [{original_id, new_id, label, run_count}]}
    API --> Browse: 200 {ok: true, imported: [...]}
    Browse -> Browse: st.cache_resource.clear() + st.rerun()
    Browse --> User: success summary + imported runs visible
end

== Re-run (UI-origin experiments only) ==
User -> Browse: select UI-origin runs -> ⚙️ Manage -> 🔄 Load spec into Setup
Browse -> API: GET /experiments/{exp_id}/spec
API -> DB: get_experiment(exp_id)
DB --> API: {spec: ExperimentSpec}
API --> Browse: {spec: {...}}
Browse -> Browse: spec_to_form_defaults(spec)
Browse -> Browse: state.setup_config = json.dumps({..._loaded_spec...})
Browse -> Browse: state.persist()
Browse --> User: success toast "Spec loaded — go to Setup"
Browse -> Setup: st.page_link("pages/8_Setup.py")

== Setup pre-populated ==
Setup -> Setup: extract_loaded_spec(setup_config)
Setup -> Setup: pre-populate all 8 tabs
Setup --> User: banner "📋 Loaded spec from experiment '...'"
User -> Setup: review params, modify budget/seeds, submit
Setup -> API: POST /experiments (origin='ui')
note right of API: new experiment ID\nnew queue entry\nnew run dirs
API --> Setup: 201 {id, status="queued"}
Setup --> User: success + navigate to Queue

@enduml
